  "instruction": "Using Jupyter Notebook, create a notebook named `iris_redundant_features.ipynb` in `/home/user/analysis_results/`. The dataset `iris-data.csv` is already present in that directory. In the notebook, load the data using pandas, compute the Pearson correlation matrix among all numeric columns (sepal length, sepal width, petal length, petal width), and identify feature pairs where the absolute correlation exceeds 0.9 (indicating redundancy). Write all redundant feature names to a text file `redundant_features.txt`, one pair per line, separated by a comma.",
